## What this predicate means

**Actor A `belongs-to` Organization B** — typed-edge predicate for actor-organization membership.  B is an entity that groups actors: employer, community, project, research-partnership, formal organization.  Multi-arity — a single actor may belong to multiple organizations (employee + community contributor + project member).  Per `decisions/actor_as_first_class_type_2026_05_11.md` Dan-directive.

## Substrate identity

- **Slot ident**: `{{predicate-ident}}`
- **Domain**: `{{domain}}`
- **Range**: `{{range}}`
- **Cardinality**: `{{cardinality}}`
- **`:dt/type`**: `:dt/DirectedBinaryRelationProperty` (asymmetric + irreflexive)

## Formal signature

`{{predicate-name}} : {{domain}} × {{range}} → Bool`

## Characteristics

- **Asymmetric** — actor belongs to org doesn't imply org belongs to actor (OWL 2 RL `prp-asyp`)
- **Irreflexive** — no entity belongs to itself (OWL 2 RL `prp-irp`)
- **NOT transitive** — org-of-org chains aren't valid memberships

## When to use belongs-to

Use on actor memorials to record organizational memberships:

```yaml
type: human-actor
name: Dan Lentz
belongs-to:
  - organizations/anthropic.md
  - organizations/clojurians.md
```

The authoritative direction is the actor side; the organization side's `has-member` inverse is derivable via inverse-of entailment.

